{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 60, :comments ["<b>Avidan son of Gid'oni.</b> This alludes to Saul, who is called אבי (my father), for so David called him (I Samuel 24:12): ״וְאָבִי רְאֵה גַּם רְאֵה״ — Dan, who was judged to have the kingdom lopped off (לִגְדֹּעַ) from him, as it says (I Samuel 15:28): ״קָרַע ה׳ אֶת מַמְלְכוּת יִשְׂרָאֵל מֵעָלֶיךָ״. Further, it may allude to Mordecai, who destroyed (אִבֵּד) the seed of Amalek. <b>Son of Gid'oni</b> — son of the one whose kingdom was lopped off (נִגְדְּעָה) — that of Saul — for his sake."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:43.976200096Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}